{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The keystone arch is an ancient architectural feature. It is composed of congruent isosceles trapezoids fitted together along the non-parallel sides, as shown. The bottom sides of the two end trapezoids are horizontal. In an arch made with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> trapezoids, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the angle measure in degrees of the larger interior angle of the trapezoid. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/c/dec895c3ce8d2cb187b83306a03e47ef6abc8f75.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(4mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); int i; real r=5, R=6;  path t=r*dir(0)--r*dir(20)--R*dir(20)--R*dir(0); for(i=0; i&lt;9; ++i) { draw(rotate(20*i)*t); } draw((-r,0)--(R+1,0)); draw((-R,0)--(-R-1,0)); [/asy]\" width=\"268\" height=\"115\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4b3480273496fadbc81016c1c5978a7f2450f48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 100 \\qquad \\text{(B) } 102 \\qquad \\text{(C) } 104 \\qquad \\text{(D) } 106 \\qquad \\text{(E) } 108$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"421\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend all the legs of the trapezoids. They will all intersect in the middle of the bottom side of the picture, forming the situation shown below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8cd92c472bdeba95f38b0309708383757b3551.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(6mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)); int i; real r=5, R=6;  path t=r*dir(0)--r*dir(20)--R*dir(20)--R*dir(0); for(i=0; i&lt;9; ++i) { draw(rotate(20*i)*t); } draw((-r,0)--(R+1,0)); draw((-R,0)--(-R-1,0));  for (int i=1; i&lt;9; ++i) draw( (0,0) -- (rotate(20*i)*(r,0)), dotted );  label(&quot;$X$&quot;,(0,0),S); label(&quot;$Y$&quot;,(R,0),SE); label(&quot;$Z$&quot;,rotate(20)*(R,0),ENE);  draw( arc( (0,0), (1.5,0), rotate(20)*(1.5,0) ) ); label(&quot;$20^\\circ$&quot;, rotate(10)*(1.75,0), E ); [/asy]\" width=\"398\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p>Each of the angles at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d03421cfd2273a966d98f778465237ef3378211b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180^\\circ}9 = 20^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/3/3039f01ba9e41f5490b7130e344be554015a25b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle XYZ$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, the degree measure of the smaller interior angle of the trapezoid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e00302c1df47bfe4fcca5a9bd28ac899d90be48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180^\\circ - 20^\\circ}2 = 80^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"135\" height=\"37\" />, hence the degree measure of the larger interior angle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/8896e588f37d8ca2faac9f29ff5f6c2051a5512c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ - 80^\\circ = \\boxed{100^\\circ \\Longrightarrow A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"206\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Proof that all the extended trapezoid legs intersect at the same point: It is sufficient to prove this for any pair of neighboring trapezoids. For two neighboring trapezoids, the situation is symmetric according to their common leg, therefore the extensions of both outside legs intersect the extension of the common leg at the same point, Q.E.D.\n</p><p>Knowing this, we can now easily see that the intersection point must be on the bottom side of our picture, as it lies on the bottom leg of the rightmost trapezoid. And by symmetry the point must be in the center of this side.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A decagon can be formed from the trapezoids and the base. The sum of the decagon's angles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/d/35d7a73a9df398a966b792ad458b3a013e8ee6af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180(10-2)=1440^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />. Letting the larger angle in each trapezoid be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the two angles formed by the line each measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e902510dbcdccbf0d866093439244571b6ca910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(180-x)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> congruent angles left. Each of those angles measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1978a1bad0a2d20ac27755ff0af3ee11cda98a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(360-2x)^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" />.  Putting it all together: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/f/f9ffad168a18e251ec5af8ec18e82df120b30a6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8(360-2x)+2(180-x)=1440\\implies x=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(A)\\ }100^\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"422\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If we reflect the arch across the line, we form an 18-gon. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/95176df4f25afe29e71949311a5319c60105445e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180*(18-2)}{18} = 160^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"169\" height=\"39\" /> so each interior angle of the 18-gon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63be0ca7bec77e7bfa985d3b42861959609e23f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$160^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> be the degree measure of the larger interior angle of a trapezoid. From the diagram, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404ff5678c02526a4180373ad452018421e11040.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 160 = 360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/1/6a1d42035a5da86f1a517feb1ae796490220daf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x = 200$\" width=\"70\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6bb5e1c9a17bddebd0a3a1dff2cddca20768d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6eb65962292d994ce2f9a8af63728883f256b18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"27\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=1914\">https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=1914</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">Problem 25</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145327\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.065 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 225/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5173/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.470      1 -total\n 59.82%    8.656      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 39.30%    5.686      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7954:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017145327 and revision id 186776. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}